From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:29:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] uboot-rockchip: configure without asking

A configuration fragment that brings up an int or hex symbol without a
default makes U-Boot's build ask for it for ever. The fragment's merge
pipes `yes ""` into `make oldconfig`, and an empty answer is no value
for such a symbol, so it is asked again; were the merge to end, every
oldconfig or syncconfig after it would ask again at the end of its
input, as the oldconfig after scripts/config in include/u-boot.mk does.
Turning on a second environment copy on a defconfig that keeps the
environment in flash does it (ENV_ADDR_REDUND), and the build's log of
the question grows without end.

Backport the two Linux fixes U-Boot's Kconfig lacks: the merge runs
olddefconfig (3266c806dc86), and such a symbol defaults to zero
(6262afa10ef7). Both are meant for U-Boot upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile          |  2 +-
 ...olddefconfig-after-merging-fragments.patch | 33 +++++++++
 ...zero-if-int-hex-symbol-lacks-default.patch | 68 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/120-kconfig-run-olddefconfig-after-merging-fragments.patch
 create mode 100644 package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/121-kconfig-default-to-zero-if-int-hex-symbol-lacks-default.patch

diff --git a/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile
index 683cb40..4061ead 100644
--- a/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile
+++ b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/Makefile
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 include $(INCLUDE_DIR)/kernel.mk
 
 PKG_VERSION:=2026.10
-PKG_RELEASE:=1
+PKG_RELEASE:=2
 PKG_HASH:=3f856da3cbbc93af51ff95fde18588a348b4a26723b01d9841e999d988481015
 
 PKG_MAINTAINER:=Sarah Maedel <openwrt@tbspace.de>
diff --git a/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/120-kconfig-run-olddefconfig-after-merging-fragments.patch b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/120-kconfig-run-olddefconfig-after-merging-fragments.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..49409d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/120-kconfig-run-olddefconfig-after-merging-fragments.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+From 3266c806dc8692e079768ee2814498dcd6a91e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Masahiro Yamada <yamada.masahiro@socionext.com>
+Date: Wed, 5 Jun 2019 03:14:53 +0900
+Subject: [PATCH] kconfig: run olddefconfig instead of oldconfig after merging
+ fragments
+
+'make olddefconfig' is non-interactive, so we can drop 'yes'.
+The behavior is equivalent.
+
+Signed-off-by: Masahiro Yamada <yamada.masahiro@socionext.com>
+[ Linux commit 3266c806dc8692e079768ee2814498dcd6a91e61. Not equivalent
+  in U-Boot, whose Kconfig gives an int or hex symbol without a default
+  an empty value, which `yes ""` cannot answer: a defconfig with
+  CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FLASH and a fragment with CONFIG_ENV_REDUNDANT=y bring
+  up ENV_ADDR_REDUND, and the merge asks for it for ever ]
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ scripts/kconfig/Makefile | 2 +-
+ 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/scripts/kconfig/Makefile b/scripts/kconfig/Makefile
+index abc34f6..53c1b43 100644
+--- a/scripts/kconfig/Makefile
++++ b/scripts/kconfig/Makefile
+@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ configfiles=$(wildcard $(srctree)/kernel/configs/$@ \
+ %.config: $(obj)/conf
+ 	$(if $(call configfiles),, $(error No configuration exists for this target on this architecture))
+ 	$(Q)$(CONFIG_SHELL) $(srctree)/scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m .config $(configfiles)
+-	+$(Q)yes "" | $(MAKE) -f $(srctree)/Makefile oldconfig
++	$(Q)$(MAKE) -f $(srctree)/Makefile olddefconfig
+ 
+ PHONY += kvmconfig
+ kvmconfig: kvm_guest.config
diff --git a/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/121-kconfig-default-to-zero-if-int-hex-symbol-lacks-default.patch b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/121-kconfig-default-to-zero-if-int-hex-symbol-lacks-default.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..78d9a1a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/boot/uboot-rockchip/patches/121-kconfig-default-to-zero-if-int-hex-symbol-lacks-default.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+From 6262afa10ef7cc8fdf39b81a36f9546b68810431 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Masahiro Yamada <masahiroy@kernel.org>
+Date: Sun, 26 Nov 2023 01:35:59 +0900
+Subject: [PATCH] kconfig: default to zero if int/hex symbol lacks default
+ property
+
+When a default property is missing in an int or hex symbol, it defaults
+to an empty string, which is not a valid symbol value.
+
+It results in an incorrect .config, and can also lead to an infinite
+loop in scripting.
+
+Use "0" for int and "0x0" for hex as a default value.
+
+Signed-off-by: Masahiro Yamada <masahiroy@kernel.org>
+Reviewed-by: Yoann Congal <yoann.congal@smile.fr>
+[ Linux commit 6262afa10ef7cc8fdf39b81a36f9546b68810431. U-Boot's
+  sym_calc_value() starts a number from symbol_empty, so its int and hex
+  cases set the tristate as well. Without it, an oldconfig or syncconfig
+  that reads no input asks such a symbol for ever, as one does after a
+  build adjusts a merged .config with scripts/config ]
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ scripts/kconfig/symbol.c | 20 ++++++++++++++------
+ 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/scripts/kconfig/symbol.c b/scripts/kconfig/symbol.c
+index 5245804..7905c1c 100644
+--- a/scripts/kconfig/symbol.c
++++ b/scripts/kconfig/symbol.c
+@@ -343,7 +343,13 @@ void sym_calc_value(struct symbol *sym)
+ 
+ 	switch (sym->type) {
+ 	case S_INT:
++		newval.val = "0";
++		newval.tri = no;
++		break;
+ 	case S_HEX:
++		newval.val = "0x0";
++		newval.tri = no;
++		break;
+ 	case S_STRING:
+ 		newval = symbol_empty.curr;
+ 		break;
+@@ -753,15 +759,17 @@ const char *sym_get_string_default(struct symbol *sym)
+ 		case yes: return "y";
+ 		}
+ 	case S_INT:
++		if (!str[0])
++			str = "0";
++		break;
+ 	case S_HEX:
+-		return str;
+-	case S_STRING:
+-		return str;
+-	case S_OTHER:
+-	case S_UNKNOWN:
++		if (!str[0])
++			str = "0x0";
++		break;
++	default:
+ 		break;
+ 	}
+-	return "";
++	return str;
+ }
+ 
+ const char *sym_get_string_value(struct symbol *sym)
